window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p>Fate, Fortune, Fame: Pick One</p> <p>I’m being paraded like a prize.</p> <p>A strategic marriage to a powerful man who wants to use me like a billboard.</p> <p>Smile for the cameras. Memorize his politics.</p> <p>Don’t slip up. Don’t speak out.</p> <p>But I already belong to someone else.</p> <p>Rhaim Selvaggio is dangerous.</p> <p>My father’s business partner. My former boss.</p> <p>The only man who’s ever made me feel safe—Even when he’s got blood on his hands.</p> <p>Especially then.</p> <p>He told me to trust him.</p> <p>To play the game.</p> <p>To wait for him to burn it all down.</p> <p>But if he didn’t want me to save myself—He shouldn’t have given me the matches.</p> <p><i>Love Her </i>is like if the movie <i>Secretary </i>met the TV shows <i>Succession </i>and <i>The Sopranos</i>, with a Beauty and the Beast themed twist. It is the second book in Cassie Alexander's The Moth and the Monster series, which marks her stunning contemporary debut.</p>"; 
